<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Red Soil</title>

    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/backend.css">
</head>

<body>

<div class="page">
    <%- include("partials/header") %>

    <div class="main">
        <%- include("partials/sidebar") %>

        <section class="blackbox">

            <h1>🌱 Red Soil – Summary</h1>
            <figure>
            <img src="https://img2.exportersindia.com/product_images/bc-full/2018/10/4775325/red-soil-1539079496-4374337.jpg" alt="RED SOIL" width="10%" height="20%">
        <figcaption><h3> fig : Red Soil </h3></figcaption>    
        </figure>
            <p>
                Red soil is common in India (Tamil Nadu, Karnataka, Andhra Pradesh,
                Telangana, Odisha, Chhattisgarh). Its red color is due to iron.
            </p>

            <h2>🔴 Characteristics of Red Soil</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>Light to medium texture</li>
                <li>Well-drained</li>
                <li>Low in nitrogen & phosphorus</li>
                <li>Rich in iron</li>
                <li>Slightly acidic to neutral</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>🌾 Crops Suitable for Red Soil</h2>

            <b>1️⃣ Groundnut (Peanut)</b>
            <ul>
                <li>Season: Kharif & Rabi</li>
                <li>Rainfall: 50–75 cm</li>
                <li>Temperature: 20–30°C</li>
                <li>Growth Duration: 90–120 days</li>
                <li>Why suitable: Loose, well-drained soil</li>
                <li>Uses: Oil, food, fodder</li>
            </ul>

            <b>2️⃣ Millets (Jowar, Bajra, Ragi)</b>
            <ul>
                <li>Season: Kharif</li>
                <li>Rainfall: 40–75 cm</li>
                <li>Temperature: 25–35°C</li>
                <li>Growth Duration: 90–110 days</li>
                <li>Why suitable: Drought-resistant</li>
                <li>Uses: Food grains</li>
            </ul>

            <b>3️⃣ Cotton</b>
            <ul>
                <li>Season: Kharif</li>
                <li>Rainfall: 60–100 cm</li>
                <li>Temperature: 21–30°C</li>
                <li>Growth Duration: 160–200 days</li>
                <li>Uses: Textile industry</li>
            </ul>

            <b>4️⃣ Pulses (Red Gram, Green Gram, Black Gram)</b>
            <ul>
                <li>Season: Kharif / Rabi</li>
                <li>Rainfall: 50–70 cm</li>
                <li>Temperature: 20–30°C</li>
                <li>Growth Duration: 70–120 days</li>
                <li>Improve soil fertility</li>
            </ul>

            <b>5️⃣ Tobacco</b>
            <ul>
                <li>Season: Rabi</li>
                <li>Rainfall: 50–100 cm</li>
                <li>Temperature: 20–30°C</li>
                <li>Growth Duration: 120–150 days</li>
            </ul>

            <b>6️⃣ Maize</b>
            <ul>
                <li>Season: Kharif</li>
                <li>Rainfall: 50–100 cm</li>
                <li>Temperature: 21–27°C</li>
                <li>Growth Duration: 90–110 days</li>
                <li>Uses: Food, fodder, starch</li>
            </ul>

            <b>7️⃣ Potato</b>
            <ul>
                <li>Season: Rabi</li>
                <li>Rainfall: 50–75 cm</li>
                <li>Temperature: 15–20°C</li>
                <li>Growth Duration: 90–120 days</li>
            </ul>

            <b>8️⃣ Oilseeds (Sesame, Sunflower)</b>
            <ul>
                <li>Season: Kharif / Rabi</li>
                <li>Rainfall: 40–60 cm</li>
                <li>Temperature: 20–30°C</li>
                <li>Growth Duration: 80–100 days</li>
                <li>Uses: Edible oils</li>
            </ul>

            <b>9️⃣ Fruits (Mango, Guava, Banana)</b>
            <ul>
                <li>Season: Perennial</li>
                <li>Rainfall: 75–150 cm</li>
                <li>Temperature: 20–35°C</li>
                <li>Banana needs irrigation</li>
            </ul>

            <b>🔟 Vegetables (Tomato, Brinjal, Chillies)</b>
            <ul>
                <li>Season: All seasons</li>
                <li>Rainfall: 60–80 cm</li>
                <li>Growth Duration: 60–120 days</li>
                <li>Uses: Daily consumption</li>
            </ul>

            <hr>

            <h2>📊 Summary Table</h2>

            <table>
                <tr>
                    <th>Crop Type</th>
                    <th>Water Need</th>
                    <th>Fertility Need</th>
                    <th>Profit</th>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Millets</td>
                    <td>Low</td>
                    <td>Low</td>
                    <td>Medium</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Pulses</td>
                    <td>Low</td>
                    <td>Low</td>
                    <td>Medium</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Groundnut</td>
                    <td>Medium</td>
                    <td>Medium</td>
                    <td>High</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Cotton</td>
                    <td>Medium</td>
                    <td>High</td>
                    <td>High</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Vegetables</td>
                    <td>Medium</td>
                    <td>High</td>
                    <td>Very High</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Fruits</td>
                    <td>Medium–High</td>
                    <td>High</td>
                    <td>Very High</td>
                </tr>
            </table>

            <hr>

            <h2>📝 Final Summary</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>Red soil is best for drought-resistant crops</li>
                <li>Millets, pulses, and groundnut are most suitable</li>
                <li>Yield improves with manure and irrigation</li>
                <li>Good for both food and commercial crops</li>
            </ul>

        </section>

    </div>

</div>

</body>
</html>
